  "final_answer": "## Answer\n\n**Yes**, the Mac Mini can be configured with a GPU larger than 16-core.\n\nAccording to Apple's website (apple.com/shop/buy-mac/mac-mini), the Mac Mini is available with two chip options:\n\n1. **M6 chip** — 12-core CPU, 12-core GPU (no larger GPU option available)\n\n2. **M5 Pro chip** — 2 options with 16-core Neural Engine:\n   - **15-core CPU, 16-core GPU** (Included / default)\n   - **18-core CPU, 20-core GPU** (available as an upgrade — \"Boost your processing and graphics performance\")\n\nSo if you choose the **M5 Pro chip with the upgraded 18-core CPU option**, you can get a **20-core GPU**, which is larger than 16-core. This is the maximum GPU configuration available for the Mac Mini.\n\n**Sources verified:**\n- US site (apple.com/shop/buy-mac/mac-mini): \"18‑core CPU, 20‑core GPU\" option confirmed\n- China site (apple.com.cn/shop/buy-mac/mac-mini): same configuration confirmed (\"18 核中央处理器、20 核图形处理器\")",
